      "standardized_narrative": "At 31 December 2017 the Syndicate reported a gross opening claims outstanding balance of $527.577m (USD). Analysis of the claims development triangle indicates a net prior-year adverse development (strengthening) of approximately $24.8m (gross), driven primarily by adverse development and IBNR increases across older underwriting years (notably a large movement in the 2015 underwriting year), and influenced by both large man-made losses (marine hull losses and individual vessel sinkings, aviation losses) and natural catastrophe activity. The 2017 hurricane season (Harvey, Irma and Maria) produced significant catastrophe losses (gross c. $109m; net c. $51m) that materially affected 2017 results and reserve setting. Reserve movements by major division show material increases in gross claims outstanding for Reinsurance (Treaty), Specialty and Property, with a small release in the Marine/Aviation & Transport division.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "The movement in the net provision for claims includes a deterioration of ($9,889,984) in respect of claims outstanding at the previous year end (2016: deterioration $7,197,000).",
        "The deterioration comprises net claims including the change in claims incurred but not reported ('IBNR').",
        "a number of large losses",
        "unusually high level of large losses",
